; a `load` that adds a signature to an operator the loading file has used already (decision 19 of
; dev/todo-sorts.md, stage 1): `complex +` is above `real +`, so what the file proved about `x + 1` is read as before
load natural
real x
use x + 1 > x
load complex                    ; the overload merges with the loader's signature on `real`
complex z
use z + x = x + z
use x + 1 > x                   ; still a `real` term: `>` takes it
expect "TypeError" "must have sort `real`"
    use z + 1 > x
